Cell["\<\
Notice that all internal fermions are assumed to be massive Dirac particles, \
so both chiralities are present in the model. Each fermion line comes with a \
chirality flip, as it should for non-derivative operators, and the chirality \
returned by UVCompletion is the one flowing into the second vertex. The \
fermion has the opposite chirality when it is emitted at the first vertex. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.936193323950345*^9, 3.936193566370812*^9}, {
  3.936195899532955*^9, 3.936195901008064*^9}, {3.972038673021572*^9, 
  3.9720387940534*^9}, {3.972038840121255*^9, 3.972038872727682*^9}, {
  3.972126516034438*^9, 
  3.972126699724574*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"262056ba-44a5-4b8c-b060-\
d7f56fcc4993"],

Cell["\<\
In this example, there is only one UV completion with new particles of spin \
\[LessEqual] 1, all scalars here:\
\>", "Text",
