Cell[TextData[{
 "Notice that self-conjugate bosons would have no arrow on their lines at all \
since we are actually tracking charge flow rather than momentum.\nTerrible \
label placement aside, we can see by eye that there are only two different \
diagrams. To check this, we convert the edge labels into colors (so all Q \
lines get one color, all L lines get one color, all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", 
    FractionBox["1", "3"]}], "}"}]], "Output",
  CellChangeTimes->{
   3.936194351806369*^9, {3.936194397983707*^9, 3.936194415540875*^9}, 
    3.936194486076464*^9, {3.936194702807621*^9, 3.936194740742436*^9}, 
    3.936194804948459*^9, 3.936196139001511*^9, 3.959761432869382*^9, 
    3.972039601804873*^9, 3.972050007399661*^9, 3.972126922703293*^9, 
    3.972127007974421*^9, {3.9721275415896482`*^9, 3.9721275867821827`*^9}, {
    3.972127620508388*^9, 3.972127628841394*^9}},ExpressionUUID->
  "c6778a86-dd56-46ae-b5ef-230049c04efa"],
 " lines get one color,...) and then use IGraph/M to check if those colored \
directed graphs are isomorphic via the function \
CompareUVCompletionsQ[uv1,uv2]. This function first checks if uv1 and uv2 \
have the same topologies, external particles, and internal particles (after \
converting them all to particles), and only then compares the colored \
directed diagrams."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9721303384645243`*^9, 3.972130358328621*^9}, {
  3.972130418200987*^9, 3.972130697620932*^9}, {3.972130742197454*^9, 
  3.972130891174985*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4043d2bf-3423-414b-a644-\
ea8fc58a1a69"],

Cell["\<\
Need IGraph/M for graph isomorphism, just run this installer to download the \
package:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9693614138697157`*^9, 
  3.9693614387907248`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0834a698-98e5-4e04-8851-\
237abe9fca65"],

