Cell["\<\
Here are the four cases that give vanishing amplitudes in the \
constant-propagator limit. In all cases one can easily track the SU(2) \
contractions and verify that the anti-Higgs pair is forced to couple to an \
SU(2) singlet, which is antisymmetric and thus gives a vanishing amplitude:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9724867955123453`*^9, 3.972486888122319*^9}, {
  3.982161232466991*^9, 
  3.9821612363457127`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1926f506-b134-415e-9849-\
a9288e61953f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

