}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Notice that we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t have Grassmann numbers here, so an \
antisymmetric fermion amplitude shows up as symmetric, basically all Young \
tableaux are transposed. The above result then says that the amplitude is \
actually antisymmetric under uR exchange, and would thus vanish if both uR \
came from the same generation. This is of course known, the S1-tilde \
leptoquark we are looking at here has an antisymmetric coupling to up quarks.
Using this amplitude code one can check for arbitrary particle exchange \
symmetries in a given UV completion.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960883606500354*^9, 3.960883717108233*^9}, {
  3.972487965259336*^9, 3.9724880153408947`*^9}, {3.972488060406623*^9, 
  3.9724881525125847`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"038dd4e5-afee-44ca-854a-\
8d7edd586181"],

Cell["\<\
We can also confirm that this \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]amplitude\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is just a linear combination of GroupMath\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Invariants for that operator, as it should be. For the \
case above there are two different contractions of the operator,\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.959869738375046*^9, 3.9598697670300617`*^9}, 
   3.9608830102986593`*^9, {3.9608834427651873`*^9, 3.960883454853499*^9}, {
   3.972488157780443*^9, 3.972488225857478*^9}, {3.97248840373801*^9, 
   3.9724884339315434`*^9}, {3.982161433698131*^9, 
   3.982161436145419*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2a930b41-ae2a-4161-809e-\
46015a7ac526"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Invariants", "[", 
   RowBox[{"group", ",", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<uR\>\"", ",", "\"\<uR\>\"", ",", "\"\<dR\>\"", 
       ",", "\"\<eR\>\""}], "}"}], "/.", "InverseReplaceSMnames"}]}], "]"}], "//",
   "Length"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.972488440002266*^9, 3.972488441028674*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[87]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a2324ded-5a1c-4421-b858-ea16975a323a"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.972488442223484*^9, 3.9731719193102427`*^9, 
  3.97333357354685*^9, 3.973862470307556*^9, 4.004024772105136*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[87]=",ExpressionUUID->"d1018064-2b71-4c18-bea9-9a3121c286f0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["and our amplitude is proportional to the second one:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.972488445378111*^9, 
  3.972488459803885*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"53c2bd1c-3b36-4559-abb8-\
25da1d43966c"],

